the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/washington/pacific-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, July to August is the driest pair on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids at 2.89 inches normal, and it came in under 90% of normal in 39 of the 75 years since 1951. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 25% of normal for June to July and 50% for May to June. So far in 2026, March to April ran 119% of normal. Grid 31825 had its driest year in 2019 at 65% of normal.</p>"}
